From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:50:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(llama-cpp): on SYCL, a model pages by default instead of
 being refused or unloaded for

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0020-sycl-paging-is-the-default.patch).

On an Intel card that several models share, a model that does not fit
need not evict another: the xe driver moves idle models' memory to host
memory and back at their next use, tenths of a second where a load after
an unload takes seconds. For that every llama.cpp model on the card needs
the backend's Battlemage VRAM check off and its buffers cut at 2 GiB -
two environment switches that defaulted the other way, so every model
file had to carry them and a model installed without them could not page.

Both now default to paging (GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK=0,
GGML_SYCL_HOST_PINNED_MEM_2G=1). A model's own `env` still decides: either
variable set in a model file wins for that model, so one model can be held
back without another backend build. A tensor larger than 2 GiB is not
refused: it gets a buffer of its own size and moves whole.

LocalAI's memory reclaimer does not know a card may hold more than its
size: with it on, the card reads full at every tick and the least recently
used model is unloaded. A deployment that pages turns it off and lets its
own keeper decide how far over the card it goes.

No computation changes. Checked without a device, with the backend's own
ggml_sycl_get_env: unset gives the new defaults, each variable set gives
its own value, a value that is no number gives the default.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
---
 .../0020-sycl-paging-is-the-default.patch     | 77 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 77 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0020-sycl-paging-is-the-default.patch

diff --git a/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0020-sycl-paging-is-the-default.patch b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0020-sycl-paging-is-the-default.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..777d132
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0020-sycl-paging-is-the-default.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+sycl: paging is the default - the Battlemage VRAM check off, buffers of 2 GiB at most
+
+On a card several models share, a model that does not fit need not push
+another one off: the xe driver moves idle models' memory to host memory and
+back at their next use (Intel Arc Pro B70: 0.2-0.4 s more on a small
+model's next request, 1.3-1.8 s on a 35B, against 7.5-8.7 s for a load
+after an unload; a card committed 3.5 GiB over its size kept every model
+loaded).
+
+That takes two things of EVERY model on the card, and both defaulted the
+other way, so each model's environment had to carry them and a model added
+without them could not page:
+
+- GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK now defaults to 0. With the check, a load the
+  card cannot hold is refused by the backend before the driver is asked;
+  the check exists because the driver does not refuse, which is exactly
+  what paging uses.
+- GGML_SYCL_HOST_PINNED_MEM_2G now defaults to 1: buffers of 2 GiB at
+  most, so that a model leaves the card in pieces and not whole (a
+  translation model without it lost 5.4 GiB at once).
+
+A model's own environment still decides, as before: GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK=1
+brings the check back for that model, GGML_SYCL_HOST_PINNED_MEM_2G=0 its
+large buffers. A tensor larger than 2 GiB is not refused either way: the
+allocator starts a new buffer only when ADDING a tensor would pass the
+maximum, so such a tensor gets a buffer of its own, of its own size, and
+that one piece moves whole.
+
+No computation changes: where a buffer ends is not what is computed in it.
+Whoever decides how far a card may be committed over its size, and that
+the host has the memory, is the caller's keeper, not the backend.
+
+Checked without a device: with the backend's own ggml_sycl_get_env, unset
+gives 0 and 1, each variable set in the environment gives its own value,
+and a value that is no number gives the default.
+---
+diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+index 1aa0170..67cafad 100644
+--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
++++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+@@ -157,9 +157,9 @@ int g_ggml_sycl_enable_flash_attention = 1;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_dev2dev_memcpy = DEV2DEV_MEMCPY_SYCL;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_usm_system = 0;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_reorder_experts = 1;
+-int g_ggml_sycl_bmg_vram_check = 1;
++int g_ggml_sycl_bmg_vram_check = 0;      // paging is the default: see where it is read
+ int g_ggml_sycl_enable_host_pinned_mem = 1;
+-int g_ggml_sycl_host_pinned_mem_2g = 0;
++int g_ggml_sycl_host_pinned_mem_2g = 1;  // paging is the default: see where it is read
+ int g_ggml_sycl_upload_staging_slots = 4;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_get_mem_api = MEMORY_API_TYPE_LEVEL_ZERO;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_enable_sparse_fa = 0;
+@@ -492,12 +492,22 @@ static void ggml_check_sycl() try {
+ 
+         g_ggml_sycl_usm_system = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM", 0);
+         g_ggml_sycl_reorder_experts = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS", 1);
+-        g_ggml_sycl_bmg_vram_check = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK", 1);
++        // PAGING IS THE DEFAULT. On a card that several models share, a model that does not fit is not refused and
++        // nothing is unloaded for it: the driver moves the idle models' memory to host memory and back at their
++        // next use (xe, Battlemage: 0.2-0.4 s on a small model's next request against 7.5-8.7 s after an unload).
++        // That takes two things of every model, and both defaulted the other way:
++        //  - the engine's own VRAM check off - with it a load the card cannot hold is refused here, before the
++        //    driver is asked (the check exists because the driver does NOT refuse, which is what paging uses);
++        //  - buffers of 2 GiB at most, so that a model leaves the card in pieces and not whole.
++        // A model's own environment still decides: GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK=1 brings the check back for it, and
++        // GGML_SYCL_HOST_PINNED_MEM_2G=0 its large buffers. (A tensor larger than 2 GiB is not refused either way:
++        // the allocator gives it a buffer of its own, of its own size, and that one piece moves whole.)
++        g_ggml_sycl_bmg_vram_check = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK", 0);
+         g_ggml_sycl_enable_host_pinned_mem =
+             ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_HOST_PINNED_MEM", 1);
+ 
+         g_ggml_sycl_host_pinned_mem_2g =
+-            ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_HOST_PINNED_MEM_2G", 0) & g_ggml_sycl_enable_host_pinned_mem;
++            ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_HOST_PINNED_MEM_2G", 1) & g_ggml_sycl_enable_host_pinned_mem;
+         g_ggml_sycl_upload_staging_slots = std::max(0, ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_UPLOAD_STAGING_SLOTS", 4));
+ 
+         g_ggml_sycl_enable_sparse_fa = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_SPARSE_FA", 0);
